WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.880
Series Smaller Than An Atom Season 1 Episode 1

00:04.880 --> 00:10.680
Imagine something so small that a million of them could fit across the diameter of a human hair.

00:10.680 --> 00:12.280
That's an atom for you.

00:12.280 --> 00:17.800
It's a tiny world, far smaller than any grain of sand or speck of dust you've ever seen.

00:17.800 --> 00:24.400
In fact, if you try to picture it, you'll probably find it impossible because the scale is simply mind-boggling.

00:24.400 --> 00:26.960
Let's take a journey into the atomic realm.

00:26.960 --> 00:28.680
Picture a grain of sand.

00:28.720 --> 00:31.960
Now, shrink that down about a hundred thousand times.

00:31.960 --> 00:35.560
You're still not quite there, but you're getting closer.

00:35.560 --> 00:41.760
Atoms are the building blocks of matter, the very foundation of everything we see, touch and experience.

00:41.760 --> 00:46.160
They compose the air we breathe, the food we eat, and even our own bodies.

00:46.160 --> 00:52.440
Yet, despite their infinitesimal size, atoms are far from being the smallest things in existence.

00:52.480 --> 00:58.680
Atoms are the tiniest pieces of the universe we live in, but there's an even smaller world waiting to be explored.

00:58.680 --> 01:06.040
Now, let's dive deeper into the world smaller than atoms, the realm of microparticles.

01:06.040 --> 01:09.440
Microparticles, as their name suggests, are tiny.

01:09.440 --> 01:14.560
So small, in fact, that they easily slip under the radar of our naked eye.

01:14.560 --> 01:16.720
But don't let their size fool you.

01:16.720 --> 01:18.720
They pack quite a punch.

01:18.720 --> 01:26.960
To put things into perspective, if an atom were the size of an apple, a microparticle would be about as small as a grain of salt.

01:26.960 --> 01:31.720
These particles are unique, not only in their size, but also in their properties.

01:31.720 --> 01:37.720
They are a part of the quantum world, a place where traditional rules of physics don't always apply.

01:37.720 --> 01:40.880
Here, particles can exist in two places at once.

01:40.880 --> 01:47.320
They can teleport through barriers, and they can even be entangled with the state of one affecting the other,

01:47.320 --> 01:49.320
no matter the distance.

01:49.320 --> 01:54.760
Now you might be thinking, that's all well and good, but what does this have to do with me?

01:54.760 --> 01:59.640
Well, these microparticles are all around us and within us.

01:59.640 --> 02:06.160
They're in the air we breathe, the food we eat, the gadgets we use, and even in the stars we gaze upon at night.

02:06.160 --> 02:10.840
They're an integral part of our daily lives, whether we realize it or not.

02:10.840 --> 02:15.600
Microparticles might be minuscule, but their role in the universe is anything but.

02:15.600 --> 02:19.840
The impact of these invisible particles is truly gigantic.

02:19.840 --> 02:26.240
Now you might be wondering, how can something so tiny have such a colossal influence on our world?

02:26.240 --> 02:28.720
Well, allow me to paint a picture for you.

02:28.720 --> 02:32.880
Microparticles are the unsung heroes of our modern world.

02:32.880 --> 02:40.600
These minuscule entities play a pivotal role in a wide array of fields, from technology to medicine to even the environment.

02:40.600 --> 02:42.880
Take a look at the world of technology.

02:42.880 --> 02:47.840
The evolution from bulky computers to sleek smartphones that fit into our pockets

02:47.840 --> 02:52.680
is largely due to the understanding and manipulation of microparticles.

02:52.680 --> 03:00.800
These tiny particles allow for miniaturization, enabling us to pack millions of transistors into a single chip.

03:00.800 --> 03:08.520
They're the reason we can carry powerful computers in our pockets and have instant access to the world's information at our fingertips.

03:08.560 --> 03:13.160
But the influence of microparticles doesn't stop at technology.

03:13.160 --> 03:16.800
They're also revolutionizing the field of medicine.

03:16.800 --> 03:23.600
Nanoparticles, a type of microparticle, are used to deliver drugs to specific cells in the body,

03:23.600 --> 03:28.080
enhancing the effectiveness of treatments and reducing side effects.

03:28.080 --> 03:33.760
Through this, we're able to fight diseases with unprecedented precision and efficacy.

03:33.760 --> 03:36.080
And let's not forget about the environment.

03:36.080 --> 03:39.720
Microparticles play a crucial role in our climate system.

03:39.720 --> 03:45.680
They're involved in cloud formation, affecting rainfall patterns and the Earth's temperature.

03:45.680 --> 03:52.760
Understanding these particles helps us predict and tackle climate change, one of the most pressing issues of our time.

03:52.760 --> 03:59.520
So next time you think about the world around you, remember there's a much smaller yet incredibly powerful world hidden within.

03:59.520 --> 04:08.560
That world is made of microparticles, invisible to the naked eye, but with an influence that reverberates throughout our lives and the universe.

04:08.560 --> 04:15.560
That's the fascinating world of microparticles, tiny, invisible, but with a colossal impact on our lives and the universe.

